2 CONT *'''Lorenzo II de Medici, Duca di Urbino (1)
2 CONT *'''M, #113660, b. 9 September 1492, d. 4 May 1519
2 CONT *Last Edited=4 Jun 2010
2 CONT *'''     Lorenzo II de Medici, Duca di Urbino was born on 9 September 1492. He was the son of Piero II de Medici and Alfonsina Orsini. He married Madeleine de la Tour, daughter of Jean III de la Tour, Comte d'Auvergne and Jeanne d
2 CONC e Bourbon, on 2 May 1518. A contract for the marriage of Lorenzo II de Medici, Duca di Urbino and Madeleine de la Tour was signed on 16 January 1517/18.3 He died on 4 May 1519 at age 26.
2 CONT *'''     He gained the title of Duca di Urbino.1 He held the office of Governor of Florence in 1513.4
2 CONT *'''Child of Lorenzo II de Medici, Duca di Urbino and Madeleine de la Tour
2 CONT **1. Catherine de Medici+ (1) b. 13 Apr 1519, d. 5 Jan 1589
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S16] Jirí Louda and Michael MacLagan, Lines of Succession: Heraldry of the Royal Families of Europe, 2nd edition (London, U.K.: Little, Brown and Company, 1999), table 67. Hereinafter cited as Lines of Succession.
2 CONT * 2.[S3409] Caroline Maubois, "re: Penancoet Family," e-mail message to Darryl Roger Lundy, 2 December 2008. Hereinafter cited as "re: Penancoet Family."
2 CONT * 3.[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 82. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT * 4.[S38] John Morby, Dynasties of the World: a chronological and genealogical handbook (Oxford, Oxfordshire, U.K.: Oxford University Press, 1989), page 108. Hereinafter cited as Dynasties of the World.
2 CONT *From: http://thepeerage.com/p11366.htm#i113660
2 CONT *_____________________________
2 CONT *'''Lorenzo II de Medici, Duke d'Urbino1
2 CONT *'''M, #80959, b. 12 September 1492, d. 4 May 1519
2 CONT *Father      Piero 'the Unfortunate' di Lorenzo de Medici, Lord of Florence2 b. 15 Feb 1471, d. 28 Dec 1503
2 CONT *Mother     Alfonsina d' Orsini2
2 CONT *'''     Lorenzo II de Medici, Duke d'Urbino was born on 12 September 1492 at Florence, Tuscany, Italy.2 A contract for the marriage of Lorenzo II de Medici, Duke d'Urbino and Madeleine de la Tour was signed on 16 January 1518.3,4
2 CONC  Lorenzo II de Medici, Duke d'Urbino died on 4 May 1519 at age 26; Died of syphilis.3
2 CONT *'''Family      Madeleine de la Tour b. c 1498, d. 28 Apr 1519
2 CONT *Child
2 CONT **Catherine d' Medici+1 b. 13 Apr 1519, d. 5 Jan 1589
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S11569] Europaische Stammtafeln, by Wilhelm Karl, Prinz zu Isenburg, Vol. II, Tafel 25.
2 CONT * 2.[S13] Worldroots.com.
2 CONT * 3.[S11569] Europaische Stammtafeln, by Wilhelm Karl, Prinz zu Isenburg, Vol. X, Tafel 95.
2 CONT * 4.[S11568] The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain, and the United Kingdom, by George Edward Cokayne, Vol. I, p. 82, notes.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p2694.htm#i80959
2 CONT *______________________
2 CONT '''Lorenzo de Medici II''' Famous memorial
2 CONT '''BIRTH	12 Sep 1492'''
2 CONT '''Florence, Città Metropolitana di Firenze, Toscana, Italy'''
2 CONT '''DEATH	4 May 1519 (aged 26)'''
2 CONT '''Careggi, Città Metropolitana di Firenze, Toscana, Italy'''
2 CONT '''BURIAL	Basilica di San Lorenzo'''
2 CONT '''Florence, Città Metropolitana di Firenze, Toscana, Italy'''
2 CONT Find a Grave Memorial ID: 91925610
2 CONT '''Italian Nobility. Known for his belonging to the influential Medici family, for being grandson''' of Lorenzo known as the Magnificent and father of the Queen of France Catherine, '''he was Lord of Florence and Duke of Urbino fr
2 CONC om 1516 to 1519. In the period before his government the influence of the his family had significantly decreased, and yet, thanks to the political and military support of the Pontifical State and more precisely of the Popes Julius
2 CONC  II and Leo X, he regained the dominion of the Tuscan Republic and the Umbrian Duchy. His tomb is considered one of Michelangelo Buonarroti's sculptural masterpieces, and his name served as inspiration for Machiavelli's essay, "th
2 CONC e Prince." '''
2 CONT Bio by: Lucy & Chris
2 CONT Family Members
2 CONT '''Parents'''
2 CONT Piero "The Unfortunate" de Medici
2 CONT 1472–1503
2 CONT
2 CONT Alfonsina Orsini
2 CONT 1472–1520
2 CONT
