1 NOTE Francis was a mental and physical weakling and was dominated by François, 
2 CONT duke of Guise, and Cardinal Charles of Lorraine, the uncles of his wife. 
2 CONT These two men, who in effect were the rulers during Francis's brief reign, 
2 CONT tried to repress the growing political power of the Protestants in France. 
2 CONT His death ended the ascendancy of the Guises at court.
