2 CONT Infanta Catherine Michelle of Spain
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine Michelle of Spain (10 October 1567 - 6 November 1597) was the youngest surviving daughter of Philip II of Spain and Elisabeth of Valois; she was also the sister of Isabella Clara Eugenia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Her paternal grandparents were Charles V, Holy Roman Emperor and Isabella of Portugal, her maternal grandparents were Henri II of France and Catherine de' Medici. Catherine Michelle never really knew her mother because Elisabeth d
2 CONC ied in 1568 when Catherine Michelle was only one year old. Her father went onto marry Catherine Michelle's cousin Anna of Austria. This marriage produced five children; among them were Philip III of Spain and Marie of Spain. Throu
2 CONC gh her father she is a descendent of Isabella of Castile, Ferdinand II of Aragon, Mary of Burgundy and Joanna of Castile.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Charles Emmanuel I, Duke of Savoy son of Emmanuel Philibert, Duke of Savoy and Margaret of France, Duchess of Berry, this marriage produced ten children, which included a son and heir for Charles Emmanuel, their childr
2 CONC en were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip (1586-1605)
2 CONT
2 CONT Victor Amadeus (1587-1637)
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry (1588-1624), Spanish Viceroy of Sicily (1622-24)
2 CONT
2 CONT Margerita (1589-1655), married Francesco IV Gonzaga of Mantua
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabella (1591-1626), married Alfonso III d'Este, duke of Modena
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas, a cardinal (1593-1657)
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie, a nun in Rome (1594-1656)
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth, a nun in Biella (1595-1640)
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Francis, Prince of Carignano (1596-1656), Founder of the House of Savoy-Carignano and ancestor of the erstwile ruling Family of Italy
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna (born 1597)
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine Michelle died near the end of 1597 while she was in Italy; she had miscarried earlier on in that year. Her father died the following year. Her sister Isabella married Albert VII, Archduke of Austria and later became Gove
2 CONC rness of the Netherlands.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Catalina Micaela von Habsburg1 F, #105009, b. 10 October 1567, d. 6 November 1597
2 CONT
2 CONT Catalina Micaela von Habsburg|b. 10 Oct 1567\nd. 6 Nov 1597|p10501.htm#i105009|Felipe II von Habsburg, Rey de España|b. 21 May 1527\nd. 13 Sep 1598|p10152.htm#i101515|Elizabeth de Valois, Princesse de France|b. 1545\nd. 1568|p1052
2 CONC 5.htm#i105247|Karl V. von Habsburg, Holy Roman Emperor|b. 24 Feb 1500\nd. 21 Sep 1558|p10152.htm#i101516|Isabel de Aviz, Infanta de Portugal|b. 4 Oct 1503\nd. 1 May 1539|p10152.htm#i101517|Henri I., Roi de France|b. 31 Mar 1519\nd
