2 CONT Full name
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Angela Caterina d'Este
2 CONT
2 CONT Father 	Borso d'Este
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother 	Ippolita d'Este
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 	1 March 1656(1656-03-01)
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 	16 July 1722 (aged 66)
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Angela Caterina d'Este (1 March 1656 – 16 July 1722) was an Italian born Princess of Modena of was later the Princess of Carignan by marriage. She was the wife of Emmanuel Philibert of Savoy the Prince of Carignan. In France
2 CONC  she was known as Angélique Catherine d'Este[1] and in Modena and Savoy she was known as Maria Caterina d'Este. She is an ancestor of Victor Emmanuel II of Italy and thus the whole present pretending Italian Royal Family. She is a
2 CONC lso an ancestor of the pretender of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Contents
2 CONT
