1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marguerite_of_Lorraine en.wikipedia.org...] ; [http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marguerite_de_Lorraine fr.wikipedia.org... ] ; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marguerite of Lorraine (22 July 1615[1] – 13 April 1672) was a princess of Lorraine by birth and duchess of Orléans by virtue of her marriage Gaston of France, younger brother of King Louis XIII. After their re-marriage, Marguerit
2 CONC e and Gaston had five children. She was the stepmother of La Grande Mademoiselle.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Life===
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born in Nancy, Lorraine to Francis II, Duke of Lorraine, and Countess Christina of Salm. One of six children, she grew up in Nancy which was the capital of her father's duchy. After losing her mother in 1627, she was broug
2 CONC ht up by her aunt Catherine of Lorraine—the Abbess of Remiremont. Two of her older brothers, Charles and Nicolas, were successively dukes of Lorraine. [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marguerite_of_Lorraine en.wikipedia.org...] ; [ht
2 CONC tp://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marguerite_de_Lorraine '''read more''']
2 CONT
2 CONT ===buried===
2 CONT Basilque Saint Denis, Saint-Denis, France.
