1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/160333499/louis-emmanuel-de_valois Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 11 2020, 15:35:36 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis-Emmanuel de Valois was the Duke of Angoulême; Earl of Lauraguais, Alais and Ponthieu; Lord of Escüen, Preaus, Tancarville,Montigny and Sezanne; Baron of Coucy and Folembray; Chevalier of the orders of the King; Colonel Gener
2 CONC al of the King's Light Horse Cavalry; and Governor of Provence.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Charles de Valois (1573-1650) and Charlotte de Montmorency. He was a grandson of King Charles IX of France and his mistress Marie Touche. He succeeded to the title of Duc d'Angoulême in 1650
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Henriette de la Guiche, Lady of Chaumont, on February 8, 1629. The children of Louis-Emmanuel and Henriette were:
2 CONT * Louis (1630-1637) Count of Auvergne;
2 CONT * Marie Françoise (1632-1696) 3rd Duchess of Angoulême;
2 CONT * Armand (1635-1639) Count of Auvergne; and
2 CONT * François (1639-1644) Count of Auvergne. In addition, he had an illegitimate son: 
2 CONT *Antoine Charles Louis (1648/49-1701), who was legitimized on 4 September 1677.
2 CONT
2 CONT The marble tomb of Louis-Emmanuel de Valois is in the church of La Guiche, France.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis-Emmanuel_d%27Angoul%C3%AAme 
2 CONT
