1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lucrezia Barberini was an Italian noblewoman. Born into the Barberini family, she was the last wife of wife of Francesco I d'Este, Duke of Modena.
2 CONT
2 CONT The eldest child of five, she was the daughter of Taddeo Barberini, Prince of Palestrina and his wife Anna Colonna herself a daughter of Filippo Colonna, Prince Colonna and Lucrezia Tomacelli. Her cousin Lorenzo Onofrio Colonna, P
2 CONC rince of Paliano was the husband of Marie Mancini.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the sister of Maffeo Barberini and Carlo Barberini and the Grand-Niece of Pope Urban VIII.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 14 October 1654 she married Francesco I d'Este, Duke of Modena and was the mother of Rinaldo d'Este, Duke of Modena. The couple married in Loreto, Marche at the Basilica della Santa Casa.
