1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Carlo Barberini was an Italian Catholic cardinal and member of the Barberini family. He was the grand-nephew of Maffeo Barberini, later Pope Urban VIII and son of Taddeo Barberini.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Taddeo Barberini, Prince of Palestrina and Anna Colonna, daughter of Don Filippo I Colonna. He was the younger brother of Lucrezia Barberini and the older brother of Don Maffeo Barberini. He was the nephew of Tad
2 CONC deo's cardinal brothers, Francesco Barberini (Senior) and Antonio Barberini and was himself the uncle of Francesco Barberini (Junior), the son of his brother Maffeo.
2 CONT
2 CONT Barberini and his younger brother Maffeo played a role in reconciling the Barberini family with the papacy (at that stage Pope Innocent X) after the Wars of Castro. Maffeo married a niece of Pope Innocent X and Carlo was elevated 
2 CONC to cardinal by Pope Innocent X in 1653.
2 CONT
2 CONT Barberini participated in 7 papal conclaves.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 2 October 1704.
