2 CONT ==Links:==
2 CONT *[http://www.thepeerage.com/p10136.htm The Peerage]
2 CONT *[http://www.geneall.net/U/per_page.php?id=4374 Geneall]
2 CONT *[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mary_II_of_England Wikipedia]
2 CONT *[http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=1978 Find a Grave]
2 CONT *'''Queen of England, Scotland and Ireland:''' Reign13 February 1689 – 28 December 1694 together with her husbond [http://www.geni.com/people/Willem-III-van-Orange-Nassau-King-of-England-Ireland-William-II-of-Scotland/600000000328
2 CONC 5553237 William of Orange]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary II (30 April 1662 – 28 December 1694) was joint Sovereign of England, Scotland, and Ireland with her husband and first cousin, William III and II, from 1689 until her death. William and Mary, both Protestants, became king and
2 CONC  queen regnant, respectively, following the Glorious Revolution, which resulted in the deposition of her Roman Catholic father, James II and VII. William became sole ruler upon her death in 1694. Popular histories usually refer to
2 CONC  their joint reign as that of "William and Mary".
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary wielded less power than William when he was in England, ceding most of her authority to him, though he heavily relied on her. She did, however, act alone when William was engaged in military campaigns abroad, proving herself 
2 CONC to be a powerful, firm, and effective ruler.
