2 CONT      Louise Adélaïde d'Orléans was born on 13 August 1698 at Versailles, Île-de-France, France. (1) 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of Philippe II d'Orléans, Duc d'Orléans and Françoise Marie de Bourbon. (1) 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on 19 February 1743 at age 44 at Priory of St. Madeleine du Trainel, rue de Charonne, Paris, France, from smallpox. (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT      Louise Adélaïde d'Orléans was also known as Mademoiselle de Chartres. (1) She was also known as Mademoiselle d'Orléans as of after 1710. (1) She was a nun on 23 August 1717 at Chelles, France. (1) She took the religious name 
2 CONC of Sister Sainte Bathilde on 23 August 1717. (1) She was the Abbess between 11 May 1719 and October 1734 at Chelles, France. (1) She was the Abbess in 1722 at Val-de-Grâce, France. (1)
