2 CONT
2 CONT Louise Élisabeth d'Orléans (11 December 1709 – 16 June 1742) was Queen Consort of Spain as the wife of Louis I. In her adopted country, she was known as Luisa Isabel de Orléans. Hers was one of the shortest reigns in European hist
2 CONC ory due to her husband's brief reign and early death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Contents
2 CONT
2 CONT [show]
2 CONT
