1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Philippe Angélique de Froissy''' (1702 – 15 October 1785 in Paris) was an illegitimate daughter of Philippe d'Orléans, the nephew and son-in-law of Louis XIV of France. She was comtesse de Ségur by marriage, and
2 CONC  a courtier of Louis XV, her cousin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her son, Philippe Henri, the maréchal de Ségur Her mother was Christine Antoinette Charlotte Desmares (1682–1753), a beautiful actress ("tragedienne") of the Théâtre-Français who was painted by Jean-Baptiste Santerre.
2 CONT
2 CONT Charlotte Desmares was a niece of Marie Champmeslé and one of the many mistresses of the regent, Philippe d'Orléans, around 1702, the year their daughter was born. Also born in 1702 was another illegitimate child of the duke, Jean
2 CONC  Philippe d'Orléans, by a lady-in-waiting, Madame d'Argenton. Angélique's half-brother was legitimised in 1706, whereas Angélique was neither acknowledged nor recognized,[2] although Madame du Prat erroneously states in her memoir
2 CONC s that she was recognized on 22 April 1722, the same day as the abbé de Saint-Albin, another illegitimate son of the Duke of Orléans by his mistress Florence Pellerin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Madame de Ségur belonged to the inner circle of Louis XV's intimates.[3] She is described as "fresh, white, well made, strong and intoxicating".[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Henri François, comte de Ségur (1689–1751) at Cagny[disambiguation needed] or Paris on 10 or 12 September 1718. He was the son Henri Joseph, comte de Ségur and Claude Élisabeth Binet.
2 CONT
2 CONT Called le beau Ségur ("the handsome Ségur"), her husband had been "master of the wardrobe" of the Regent (maître de la garderobe du Régent). He lived in an hôtel in Passy, Paris on a beautiful ten-acre property, which later passed
2 CONC  to the Duchess of Valentinois and was named Hôtel de Valentinois after her. (The property is famous for being the residence of Benjamin Franklin for nearly ten years.)[5][6]
2 CONT
2 CONT They had at least five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Philippine Charlotte de Ségur (Paris, 12 July 1719 - Paris, 12 July 1719) Henriette Élisabeth de Ségur (Paris, 20 September 1722 - 1747?), unmarried and without issue Philippe Henri, marquis de Ségur (Paris, 20 January 1724 - Pari
2 CONC s, 3 October 1801), marshal of France in 1783, twin with the below Philippe Angelique de Ségur (Paris, 20 January 1724 - Paris, 20 January 1724), twin with the above Henriette Césarine de Ségur (1726-1782), married Bertrand Gaich,
2 CONC  baron de la Crozes, Knight of Saint-Louis. Angélique died in Paris 1785 at 83 years of age, and was buried at the Église Saint-Eustache, Paris.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ang%C3%A9lique_de_Froissy
