1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * "<em>[http://www.westminster-abbey.org/our-history/people/james,-earl-of-dalkeith James Scott, Earl of Dalkeith]</em>", Westminster Abbey
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Scott,_Earl_of_Dalkeith
2 CONT
2 CONT James Scott, Earl of Dalkeith, KT (23 May 1674 – 14 March 1705) was a Scottish nobleman and politician. He was the son of James Scott, 1st Duke of Monmouth, and Anne Scott, 1st Duchess of Buccleuch. He was also the grandson of Cha
2 CONC rles II of England, Scotland and Ireland. On 2 January 1693/94 he married Lady Henrietta Hyde (born in Hindon, Wiltshire, c. 1677, died 30 May 1730), daughter of Laurence Hyde, 1st Earl of Rochester, and Henrietta Hyde, Countess o
2 CONC f Rochester. They had six children:
2 CONT
2 CONT The Hon. Francis Scott, 2nd Duke of Buccleuch (11 January 1695 – 22 May 1751) married (1) Lady Jane Douglas, daughter of James Douglas, 2nd Duke of Queensberry and Mary Boyle; (2) Alice Powell, daughter of Joseph Powell
2 CONT Lady Anne Scott (1 April 1696 – 11 October 1714)
2 CONT Lady Charlotte Scott (30 April 1697 – 22 August 1747)
2 CONT The Hon. Charles Scott (March 1700 – 4 April 1700)
2 CONT The Hon. James Scott (14 January 1702 – 26 February 1719)
2 CONT The Hon. Henry Scott (26 November 1704 – died young)
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Dalkeith died of apoplexy and was buried 19 March 1704/05 in the King Henry VII Chapel of Westminster Abbey.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Scott-11804
2 CONT * https://dbpedia.org/page/James_Scott,_Earl_of_Dalkeith
2 CONT * https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/MSV3-DHQ/james-scott-earl-of-dalkeith-1674-1705
2 CONT * https://global.museum-digital.org/people/133458
2 CONT * https://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:James_Scott_%28172%29
2 CONT * https://familypedia.fandom.com/wiki/James_Scott_(1674-1705)
2 CONT * https://www.westminster-abbey.org/abbey-commemorations/commemorations/james-scott-earl-of-dalkeith
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/76079379/james_scott
2 CONT
2 CONT James Scott, Earl of Dalkeith was the son of James Scott, 1st and last Duke of Monmouth and Anne Scott, Countess of Buccleuch.
2 CONT He was baptised on 26 May 1674.
2 CONT He married Lady Henrietta Hyde, daughter of Laurence Hyde, 1st Earl of Rochester and Lady Henrietta Boyle, on 2 January 1693/94.
2 CONT He died on aged 30 at Albemarle Street, London, England, from apoplexy.
2 CONT He was buried on March at Westminster Abbey, Westminster, London.
2 CONT
2 CONT He fought in the Campaign in Flanders in 1692.
2 CONT He was invested as a Knight, Order of the Thistle (K.T.) on 7 February 1704.
