1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Stuarta Werburge Howard held the office of Maid of Honour to Queen Mary II. She died in 1706, unmarried; she was engaged to the 1st Earl of Portland in 1700 but the marriage never took place. This resulted in a due
2 CONC l between Portland and her stepfather, Yarmouth. 
2 CONT
2 CONT links
2 CONT * http://www.thepeerage.com/p7036.htm#i70352
2 CONT
2 CONT Alternate version:
2 CONT
2 CONT * from http://genealogy.links.org/links-cgi/readged?/home/ben/camilla-genealogy/current+c-howard1045+2-2-0-1-0
2 CONT
2 CONT Stuarta Walberga Howard, Maid of Honour to Qu. Mary II. Stuarta was apparently engaged to marry, in July 1700 as his second wife, Hans Willem Bentinck, 1st Earl of Portland, but he married someone else instead. As a result, Portla
2 CONC nd fought a duel with Stuarta's half-brother, Lord Paston.
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
