1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Fitz-James_Stuart,_2nd_Duke_of_Berwick '''James Francis Fitzjames Stuart, II. Duke of Berwick''']
2 CONT ===Golden Fleece - Knights: Spanish Branch===
2 CONT
2 CONT James FitzJames Stuart married Catalina Ventura Colón de Portugal, Duquesa de Veragua, and Duquesa de la Vega. She was a descendant of Admiral Cristóbal Colón (Christopher Columbus)..
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT James Francis (Diego Francisco) Fitz-James Stuart, 2nd Duke of Berwick, (Saint-Germain-en-Laye, France, 21 October 1696 - Naples, Italy, 2 June 1738) was a Jacobite and Spanish nobleman. He inherited titles in the Jacobite and Spa
2 CONC nish nobility on the death of his father in battle in 1734 at Philippsburg, (near Karlsruhe, presently located in the German "Bundesland" of Baden-Württemberg), during the War of the Polish Succession. He was also Consort Duke of 
2 CONC Veragua and of la Vega and a Consort-Marquis of four further titles by his Spanish marriage in 1716. His full title was 2nd Duke of Berwick, 2nd Earl of Tinmouth, 2nd Baron Bosworth, 2nd Duke of Liria and Xerica, Grandee of Spain 
2 CONC 1st class (from 1716), '''Knight of the Order of the Golden Fleece (from 29 September 1714)''', as well as the holder of several earldoms.
