1 NOTE The patriarch of the family was Francois Marie De Reggio, an Italian whocame to Louisiana in 1751 with a commission from the King of France toestablish two forts: the Fort of Baton Rouge and the Fort of Arkansas. Hethen acted as t
2 CONC he negotiator for the King of France to sell the LouisianaTerritory to the Spanish, afterward becoming the standard bearer for theSpanish king. In 1803, hearing that Spain had secretly ceded theLouisiana Territory back to France, 
2 CONC President Thomas Jefferson purchasedit from Napoleon for $15 million and doubled the size of the United States
2 CONT
