2 CONT * '''Maria Vittoria's parents'''
2 CONT * D1. '''Don Giulio Cesare''', 5th Prince of Carbognano, Prince of Anticoli and Roviano, Duke of Bassanello, Nerola and Montelibretti, Lord Castelnuovo etc. (1750-87), Great of Spain I class, Prince of Palestrina maritali nomine, 
2 CONC *13.5.1702, +Roma 28.1.1787; m.1728 '''Donna Cornelia Constanza Barberini''' 4th Princess of Palestrina, Lady of Capranica Prenestina, Monte Castel San Pietro and Castelvecchio, daughter and heiress of Prince Don Urbano and Prince
2 CONC ss Donna Maria Teresa Boncompagni from Dukes of Sora (*21.12.1716, +7.12.1797) 
2 CONT * '''Maria Vittoria & her siblings'''
2 CONT * E1. Donna Olimpia Colonna, *Roma 1.11.1731, +Roma 22.12.1800; m.1748 (separated) Don Gennaro Caracciolo Duke of Girifalco
2 CONT * E2. Don Urbano Colonna, take the surname Barberini Colonna di Sciarra, 6th Prince of Carbognano, Prince of Roviano, Duke of Bassanello, Nerola and Montelibretti, Count of Palazzuolo, Lord and Baron of Santo Stefano, Count of Pac
2 CONC entro, Count degli stati di Lucoli, Rojo and Tornimparte, Baron and Lord of Rocca di Santo Stefano, Sant'Eusanio, Fossa, Casentino, Bassano, Monticchio, Villa Sant'Angelo, Tusillo, Stizze, Rocca di Mezzo, Rocca di Cambio, della fo
2 CONC nte d'Avignone and della valle di Pagliano subaequo from 1787, Great of Spain I, *16.6.1733, +Napoli 8.2.1796; m.1770 Donna Monica Carafa, dau.of Don Ettore 11th Duke of Andria, Marques of Corato, Prince of Chiusano by Donna Franc
2 CONC esca de Guevara from Dukes of Bovino
2 CONT * E3. Donna Anna Maria Colonna; m.1749 Don Filippo I Sforza Cesarini 5th Duke Sforza Cesarini, Duke of Fiano, Prince of Genzano, Marques of Proceno and Count of Santa Fiora (*1727, +1764)
2 CONT * E4. Don Carlo Colonna, 5th Prince of Palestrina, Lord of Monte Castel San Pietro, Capranica Prenestina and Castel Vecchio, Great of Spain I class (1787-1819), take the surname Colonna Barberini, *5.9.1735, +1819; m.4.11.1770 Don
2 CONC na Giustina Borromeo Arese (*3.12.1746 +1815)
2 CONT * E5. '''Donna Maria Vittoria Felice Colonna''', +20.7.1817; m.4.10.1758 Don Bartolomeo Corsini 3th Prince of Sismano, 2nd Duke of Casigliano, Marques of Lajatico, Count Palatine and Marques of Orciano (*1729, +1792)
