1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emmanuel_Thomas,_Count_of_Soissons
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince Thomas Emmanuel of Savoy, (8 December 1687 – 28 December 1729), was born a prince of Savoy and was later Count of Soissons from 1702 till his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Prince Louis Thomas of Savoy (1657–1702) and Uranie de La Cropte.
2 CONT  The famous general Prince Eugene of Savoy was his uncle.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married on October 24 1713 with Princess Maria Theresia of Liechtenstein (1694-1772), Duchess of Troppau and had one son. He became a Knight in the Austrian Order of the Golden Fleece in 1712. He died in Vienna.
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue
2 CONT
2 CONT  1.Eugène-Jean-François (1714-1734), next count of Soissons and Duke of Troppau.
