1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Rev Hon Richard Henry Roper'''    
2 CONT
2 CONT * Birth: November 6, 1723   Sittingbourne, UK   
2 CONT * Death: November 1810  (87)   
2 CONT * Parents: Sir Henry Roper, 8th Baron Teynham and Anne Moore (Lennard), 16th Baroness Dacre 
2 CONT * Wife: Mary Roper 
2 CONT * Children: William lennard Roper; John Henry Roper; Henry Welladvice Roper; Caroline Roper; William Roper; The Very Rev Henry Roper; Cadwallader Blayney Trevor Roper and Richard Roper 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Rev. Hon. Richard Henry Roper was born in November 1723.[2] He was the son of Henry Roper, 8th Baron Teynham and Anne Lennard, Baroness Dacre. He married, secondly, Mary Tenison, daughter of Captain Thomas Tenison, in 1760. He mar
2 CONC ried, firstly, Hon. Mary Chetwynd, daughter of William Richard Chetwynd, 3rd Viscount Chetwynd of Bearhaven and Honora Baker, on 20 May 1755.[1] He died in November 1810.[2] He was the Rector of Clones, County Monaghan, Ireland.[3
2 CONC ]
2 CONT
2 CONT Rector of Clones for many decades. Husband of Mary Chetwynd (died at or shortly after the birth of their child Mary in 1758) and his second wife Jane Mary Tenison (seven or eight children).
