1 OCCU Médico Cirujano de la Armada Española
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Destacado Médico Cirujano de origen español, que intervino al Brigadier/Almirante de la Armada Española Cosme Damián Churruca y Elorza al ser herido en una pierna durante la Batalla de Trafalgar (1805).
2 CONT
2 CONT Su estirpe se remonta a la Reina Inés de Castro de Portugal (1320-1355), hija del conde de Lemos, bisnieta del Rey Sancho IV de Castilla y esposa del Rey Pedro I de Portugal apodado “El Justiciero”. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Prominent Spanish-born surgeon who operated on Brigadier/Admiral Cosme Damián Churruca y Elorza of the Spanish Navy after he was wounded in the leg during the Battle of Trafalgar (1805).
2 CONT
2 CONT His lineage dates back to Queen Inés de Castro of Portugal (1320-1355), daughter of the Count of Lemos, great-granddaughter of King Sancho IV of Castile and wife of King Pedro I of Portugal nicknamed “The Just”.
