0 @N6000000002322348050@ NOTE Louis's interest in improving Paris never waned, for he razed the city's
1 CONT medieval walls, built the Invalides, a home for disabled veterans, planned
1 CONT the Great Avenue of the Champs-ELysees and refurbished the Cathedral at Notre
1 CONT Dame. Much time was spent at "the showplace of Europe", a palace he had built
1 CONT in Versailles, near Paris. He ruled a war-weary France 'til his health broke
1 CONT in 1715, suffering from fever and gangrene. His final words were to have
