1 CONT Charles Radclyffe was the son of Edward Ratcliffe, 2nd Earl of Derwentwater <p10843.htm> and Mary Tudor <p10504.htm>. He was born on 3 September 1693 at Little Parndon, Essex, England. He married Charlotte Maria Livingston, daught
1 CONC er of Charles Livingston, 2nd Earl of Newburgh <p2945.htm> and Frances Brudenell <p7896.htm>, on 24 June 1724. He died on 8 December 1746 at age 53 at Tower Hill, The City, London, England, beheaded.  He gained the title of 5th Ea
1 CONC rl of Derwentwater, de jure. In 1745 he took part in the 1745 Uprising.
1 CONT Children of Charles Radclyffe and Charlotte Maria Livingston:
1 CONT James Bartholomew Radclyffe, 4th Earl of Newburgh <p7896.htm>+ b. 23 Aug 1725, d. 2 Jan 1787 Maj.-Gen. James Clement Radclyffe <p7897.htm> b. 5 Nov 1727, d. 1788 Mary Radclyffe <p7897.htm>+ b. 5 Apr 1732, d. 27 Aug 1798
1 CONT
1 CONT Charles RADCLYFFE b: 3 SEP 1693 in Little Parndon,Essex,England
1 CONT
1 CONT Name: Charles RADCLYFFE
1 CONT Sex: M
1 CONT Birth: 3 SEP 1693 in Little Parndon,Essex,England
1 CONT Death: 8 DEC 1746 in England of beheaded
1 CONT Burial: St Guiles-in-the-Fields Note:
1 CONT MARRIAGE: Charles was married to his cousin, Lady Betty Lee Linchfield, when he found out that his previous girlfriend, Margaret Snowden was with child. Charles was the forced to marry Meg by her father and brother in a shotgun we
1 CONC dding. Charles stayed with Meg long enough to give the baby, Jane, the Radclyffe name. Charles then went back to his wife, Laddy Betty, but stayed in touch with Meg and his daughter, Jane until his death.MARRIAGE: LADY CHARLOTTE M
1 CONC ARIA LIVINGSTONE Married CHARLES RADCLYFFE (56-3) on June 24, 1724, in Brussels. Lady Charlotte Maria was the Countess of Newburgh, daughter of the second Earl of Newburgh.MARRIAGE: MARGARET "MEG" SNOWDEN Married CHARLES RADCLYFFE
1 CONC  (56-3). Margaret was born in 1694, died in 1723, daughter of Jane and John Snowden, who was a common laborer. Jane Snowden died on Jan. 14, 1709. Charles was married to his cousin Lady Betty Lee Linchfield when he found out that 
1 CONC his previous girlfriend Margaret Snowden was with child. Charles then was forced to marry her by her father and brother having a shotgun wedding for them. Charles stayed with Meg long enough to give the baby a Radclyffe name. Char
1 CONC les went back to his wife Lady Betty but stayed in touch with them until his death.DEATH: Charles was beheaded at age 53 and his body buried in St. Guiles-in-the-Fields. His heart was carried to Dilson by two loyal servants where 
1 CONC it was placed in a leaden box beside the coffin of his brother James, the Fifth Earl of Derwentwater.CHILDREN: with Meg Snowden:1.Lady Jane "Jenny" (born in 1710, England-died in America) (Married Robert "Rob" Wilson on May 6, 172
1 CONC 6, at the Church of Westover, Virginia) (she came to America on April 20, 1726)CHILDREN: with LADY CHARLOTTE MARIA LIVINGSTONE:2.James Bartholomew (Aug. 23, 1725, Vincennes, near Paris, France) (Third Earl of Newburgh) (Married Ba
1 CONC rbara Kempe)3.James Clement (twin to Barbara)4.Barbara (twin to James Clement)5.Charles6.Charlotte7.Anne8.Mary (Married Francis Eyre)BIOGRAPHY: From this "Great William" ennobled successively by the titles of Baron Fitzwalter and 
1 CONC Earl of Sussex, now extinct, descended the Radcliffes, Earls of Derwentwater who suffered such a fatal eclipse on the execution of the unfortunate James, Earl of Derwentwater, for his share in the rebellion of 1715, and his no les
1 CONC s unfortunate brother Charles who had assumed the title, and who was father of another Charles who became Earl of Newburgh.
