1 CONT the Habsburg dominions, he was an "enlightened despot", and sought to
1 CONT introduce administrative, legal, economic, and ecclesiastical reforms with
1 CONT only measured success. During his reign, 700 monasteries were dissolved for
1 CONT not being engaged with useful activities as teaching or hospital work, and
1 CONT 36,000 monks were forced to leave their orders, given an annuity or money to
1 CONT return home, during which time many works of art were destroyed.
